<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Henhouse Reception</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css">
  <!-- Nothing hidden in the HTML this time. Look at the envelope, not the letter. -->
</head>
<body>
  <main class="site-main">
    <article class="auth-card" style="max-width:34rem;">
      <h1>🛎️ Henhouse Reception</h1>
      <p>
        The desk is spotless. Not a flag in sight on this page &mdash; and viewing the
        source won't help you here.
      </p>
      <p style="color:var(--ink-soft); font-size:0.95rem;">
        The receptionist clips a note to the <em>envelope</em> every request arrives in.
        Check the HTTP <strong>response headers</strong> for this page &mdash; try your
        browser's Network tab, or run:
      </p>
      <pre>curl -I <%= 'http://localhost:3000/c/header-hen/desk' %></pre>
      <p style="margin-top:1.5rem;"><a href="/challenges/header-hen">← Back to the challenge</a></p>
    </article>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
